  THE REAL COMPARISON: |F1 - target| against the BLIND controller
    BLIND (no sensor)     36.2 Hz    <- feed-forward reach alone
    SLICE bin 8           36.1 Hz      -0.1 Hz against blind
    weighted 32           32.6 Hz      -3.6 Hz against blind
    pop MEAN              37.2 Hz      +0.9 Hz against blind
    WRONG bin 24          37.2 Hz      +1.0 Hz against blind

  GUARD  is it INFORMATION or just inhibition?
         SLICE beats blind by +0.1 Hz, the WRONG band by -1.0 Hz
         -> NOT INFORMATION: a band with no F1 does as well, so the gain is DRIVE

  AND THE PROJECTION CHECK IS VOID as it was written. It compared
  percentages-removed-against-gain-0 to aimsense's numbers, which are
  also against gain 0 -- so both sides were dominated by feed-forward and
  the agreement or disagreement said nothing about the sensor. The
  quantity that means anything is the column above.

  REFUSED, AND IT REFUSES MORE THAN ITSELF. Against a BLIND controller
  the measured slice buys 0.1 Hz and an F1-free band buys -1.0 Hz: the
  loop is collecting DRIVE. Do not build the tract.

  AND aimsense's headline INHERITS THIS. Its ladder scored every arm
  against gain 0 and never ran a blind controller, so its 51.9% may be
  mostly reach. That result needs re-measuring against this baseline
  before it is quoted again.
